course: dictionary
lesson: 1989
title: Compromise: giving a little to agree
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compromise is a deal where each side gives up a little of what it wants, so that both can agree. «The capital of Australia is Canberra, built as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne.» Both cities wanted to be the capital, so neither got everything. Each gave a little, and the answer was a new city in between.
explain: As a verb, compromise means to settle an argument by each side giving something up. «Arguing over paint colours like "Magnolia" or "Duck Egg Blue" is a small disagreement, and it ends with a choice or a compromise.» The clues are disagreement and then choice. The word fits the idea of meeting halfway.
explain: Compromise can also mean to put something in danger or make it weaker. «You should never compromise your safety for fun.» The clue is safety: giving it up would harm you, so compromise means to weaken or endanger. Check by swapping in your meaning: "You should never weaken your safety for fun" still makes sense.
fact: A compromise is a deal where each side gets part of what it wants.
fact: Compromise can be a noun (a compromise) or a verb (to compromise).
fact: To negotiate means to talk until you find a deal that both sides can accept.
fact: «Reach a compromise» and «meet halfway» both mean finding a fair middle point.
fact: «Compromise your safety» means to put your safety in danger or make it weaker.
exercise: Mia and Sam both wanted the red bike, so they agreed to share it, half an afternoon each. What is this called? | A competition | *A compromise | A complaint | A surprise
exercise: «You should never compromise your safety for fun.» In this sentence, compromise means | To go to bed early | To shout loudly | *To put in danger or make weaker | To agree with everyone
exercise: Which word means to talk until you find a deal both sides accept? | Shout | Ignore | *Negotiate | Sneeze
test: «The capital of Australia is Canberra, built as a compromise between rival cities Sydney and Melbourne.» Why was Canberra built this way? | Sydney was far too small to be a city | *Both cities wanted to be the capital, so each side gave a little | Melbourne asked for a new airport | Canberra was built on a ship
test: Which phrase means finding a fair middle point? | *Meet halfway | Run away | Shout louder | Ask the teacher
exam: When Ana and her brother disagree about what to watch on TV, the best way to end the quarrel is to | *Make a compromise, with each giving up a little | Switch off the TV and hide the remote | Stop speaking to each other for a week | Shout until the other gives in
